---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_URL, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy policy of Aurora Tonight: your location stays yours" description="What the aurora forecast processes: no account, no cookie, location used in your browser only, coordinates sent rounded to the NWS or MET Norway for clouds. Your rights." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>This policy covers {SITE_URL}. The publisher is established in France: the EU General Data Protection Regulation applies to everything the site does, for every visitor, and residents of US states with a consumer privacy law keep at least the rights listed here.</p>
    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>2. Your location</h2>
    <p>You can pick a town from the list, type a ZIP code or coordinates, or press "Use my location", which asks your browser for your position. In every case the position is used inside the page you are viewing. It is never sent to us. To compute the answer, your browser itself sends the coordinates, rounded to four decimals or less, to the cloud forecast service: the National Weather Service (api.weather.gov, a US government service) for places in the United States, or the Norwegian Meteorological Institute (api.met.no) elsewhere or if the first does not answer. A ZIP code is converted to coordinates with a file from this site, downloaded by your browser, without sending the ZIP code anywhere.</p>
    <h2>3. What is processed by us</h2>
    <h3>Hosting logs</h3><p>Like every web host, GitHub records the IP address, time, page requested and browser type of each request to keep the service secure. Legal basis: legitimate interest. Retention follows GitHub's own policy.</p>
    {CLARITY_ID
      ? <><h3>Anonymous stability monitoring, without cookies</h3><p>To find broken pages and scripts, the site loads Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, Dublin) in its cookie-free mode: errors, loading times and clicks that lead nowhere are measured per page view, without cookies and without linking visits; page content and everything typed are masked. Legal basis: legitimate interest in a working site (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can object by blocking clarity.ms or writing to us.</p></>
      : <><h3>No analytics</h3><p>No audience measurement, analytics or advertising tool is loaded today. If one is added, this page will name it before it is switched on.</p></>}
    <h3>E-mails</h3><p>If you write to us, we keep your address and message to answer, and delete them three years after the last exchange.</p>
    <h2>4. No sale, no profiles</h2><p>We do not sell or share personal information and build no profiles. There is no account, no alert list and no advertising on the site.</p>
    <h2>5. Transfers</h2><p>The host, GitHub, Inc., is in the United States; request data may be processed there under the EU–US Data Privacy Framework. The feeds your browser calls are run by NOAA and the National Weather Service in the United States and by the Norwegian Meteorological Institute in Norway.</p>
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>You may ask for access, correction, deletion, restriction or portability, or object, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we answer within one month. You may also complain to the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl}</a>).</p>
    <h2>7. Children</h2><p>The site is not directed at children under 13 and collects nothing from them.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> and the <a href={route('terms', lang)}>legal notice</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
